 rescuing them and getting  them out safe and sound  he just watched them die and it's like  the one thing he's the most terrified of  is facing down his own past and that's a  very very very big deal because one of  the things that Williamson's been  hitting on a lot recently with his run  on the flash is fear of the past fear  the past with like iris West and the  sense that she's regaining a lot of the  memories that she had fear of the past  for Barry and the Sin City may repeat  his past mistakes these are all very  very important things very important  themes that go on with these characters  and so the result of this is that  heatwave initially just kind of lets his  guard down for a momentary second and  then lashes out again it's a defense  mechanism  it's his inability to face the reality  of the situation that this is a part of  who he is  that he led all this to happen and so  what do you attempt to do is destroy  that part of himself and flash tries to  and the reason why is because this is  really like the core part of heatwave if  he destroys this he destroys what's left  of his humanity he destroys what's left  of him or any semblance of possibly  being a good person because while this  is his lightning rod of being able to  escape back to the real world from being  trapped in his own mind it's also his  lightning rod to keep him from killing  people it's what keeps him in check if  that's destroyed who knows what kind of  person he'll become just some crazy  violent psychopathic killer  and so they concern about this with  regards to commander colt is that with  everything that goes on here the Speed  Force of Barry Allen is merging with the  sage force of heatwave and what this  means is that is amping up the sage  force and so it's kind of cool because  it means the Speed Force can can act as  a complement to the sage force in the  same way the Blue Lantern rings off  operate as a complement to the Green  Lantern rings and so with these two  things merging it means the power of the  sage force is expanding rapidly  incredibly fast and so the concern  commander colt has is if heat wave has  another kind of like outburst or another  explosion of sorts it'll eradicate all  of Central City and that's the important  thing to bear in mind here when it comes  to the sage force is that it focuses on  the the mental powers and abilities of a  particular person you know individually  and so with this happening with heat  wave having such an obsession with fire  letting off this kind of energy that's  being manifested because of the sage  force if this were to keep going say for  example Barry Allen were to die inside  the mind of heatwave then in turn the  Speed Force could potentially be trapped  in heat wave or at least Barry's portion  of it and then in turn would continue  amping amping up the sage force could go  nuclear or possibly even destroy the  world it could cause all hell break  loose and so what is up happening here  as you have commander colt who basically  freezes heatwave as best he can in the  real world nor to keep his energy from  just expanding outward to rapidly but  then iris begins to have these memories  now the memories of iris has this is  actually an interesting interesting  thing back in the 1970s and the early  1970 really around 1971 DC was looking  for a way to write iris West out but to  keep her in the back pocket and the way  to do that was to basically say she was  time-displaced  to say that iris West was actually born  in the 30th century and then was  essentially sent back in time by her  biological parents and then she was  raised by Nadine West and whatever the  husband's name was in like the 20th  century and then of course Barry ended  up meeting her it was a way to kind of  write iris out and then just see what  they could do with it later on  introduced like somebody else so of  course they wrote iris out they killed  her and then in turn that led to Barry  meeting somebody else it was an  experiment he was  test to see if Barry Allen's comics  could stand without iris but that's why  this works is because what she does is  she has memories of you know basically  memories that dr. Manhattan took away of  when she lived in the 30th century and  when she was exposed to all the  technology that was there and all the  history that was there which included  the sage force and so when she goes  through and starts analyzing all these  memories thinking about what she's  experienced and so on and so forth her  response is there's a way to get Barry  Allen out of this now remember the sage  force is still a bit ambiguous we still  don't know everything about these forces  and the reason why I say this is so  ambiguous is because what you end up  having is a sage force or this the  source of energy  that seems to grant people like  telepathy enhance their minds and so on  and so forth but when commander cold is  basically sent into the mind of heat  wave by iris West he pretends to be  captain cold and so if telepathy were a  legitimate part of the sage force you  would think it would pick up on that and  say no this guy is commander cold like  look at all the memories that he has in  his mind that I'm currently reading  about at the moment the only other way  to seem to do that that he could seem to  get around that is if you've blocked all  those memories out and the only memories  the sage force could see our memories  are really just memories he has from  like reading the stories of Captain cold  and like knowing what Captain cold did I  mean you start saying things like  remember that that that scheme that we  pulled we were in metropolis and we  basically goofed off and you know  Superman caught us and you told Superman  that he had coffee breath where Superman  probably does and like all these  different things he kind of relives  these memories and what this does is it  really kind of feeds into heat wave and  kind of brings him back to the person  that he is and says okay look you know  let's go ahead and set things to rights  and let's get out of this place let's  get back into the real world and it's  kind of cool because when when heat wave  kind of goes back to his normal self  it's the classic heat wave that we  remember it's the version with like the  the flame gun with the flamethrower gun  and you know and this this you know  really funky cool looking suit that he  has you know different little things  like that this in turn leads to the sage  force essentially like lashing out and  trying to destroy heatwave remember the  the various forces that are there the  sage force the strength force is still  force so on and so forth they're looking  for hosts they're bonding themselves to  a particular host now what Williamson  seems to be doing here is saying there  is an ideal host for each one of these  forces they just haven't found them yet  and it just happens to be that each one  of these forces are buying themselves to  like the various rogues of the flash but  it is kind of cool because what you end  up getting is like the sage force going  to attack in an intern trying to attack  Barry who basically runs in circles kind  of a throwback  the old crisis on Infinite Earths when  he sacrificed his life in order to stop  the anti-monitor  but in doing so manages to disperse the  sage force from the mind of of heatwave  and then send it back out into the  universe again now again where it goes  from here we don't know and there's no  way for berry to track it there's no way  for him to actually locate where the  sage force is he's just kind of has to  wait for it to find a new host and then  see if there's some way to basically  stop it or something on the something  along those lines again all this stuff  is new to bear he hasn't even had time  to study them yet and the only person  that really does have information about  it which is commander colt is very  hush-hush he won't tell him anything for  fear of changing the past and so in this  moment what is up happening is Barry  meets with Iris after it's all said and  done and heat waves taken back to iron  Heights and everything he ends up  meeting with iris and iris basically  says you have to do what the other  flashes told you what the other  multiversal flash has told you and go on  a force quest learn about all these  various forces that are out there and  understand them and Barry says I've  already done that and that's what I'm  going to do but the one thing that holds  him back the thing that keeps him from  doing that is iris and the reason why is  because remember up until Barry regained  his memories after touching out Wally  West who came out of the Speed Force  Barry didn't know that he and iris West  were a couple he didn't know about the  past life he didn't know about  everything before flashpoint that they  were married you know they they had the  tornado twins he didn't know about all  that kind of stuff  when the memory started flowing back to  him and when the memory started flowing  back to iris that's when he realized how  much time had been lost that's when he  realized how long they had been apart  even though they weren't supposed to do  and so his idea is I don't ever want to  leave you though like I care too much  about you I don't want to see you walk  away and her response is well you're an  idiot if you think that because I'm  coming with you which is a really cool  thing it's a really touching thing to  see iris be able to go on like this  force quest with Barry and learn about  the forces as he learns about them is  actually pretty badass I guess it's  pretty awesome and I'm pretty excited to  see it it's a good story I'm really  loving I've been loving what Joshua  Williams has been doing the flash ever  since the arts a little wonky but aside  from that like everything else seems  pretty solid but if you guys are new  here to comment explain make sure you  guys are th